{"author":{"id":"694fb8161bd8bf91df2a28db7c649e48f8c5fa47ad3ad0234607d35f0482801a"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790448295,"nonce":"uwr7WqlmwaYvxSPrtD1WJLG7j7Q=","title":"Superclass resolves to an imported class with the same name","message":"other.wren:\n```wren\nclass Box {\n  construct new(v) { _v = v }\n}\n```\nmain.wren:\n```wren\nimport \"other\" for Box as OtherBox\nclass Box {\n  construct new(v) { _v = v }\n  name { \"instance\" }\n}\nclass Plain is Box {\n  construct new(v) { super(v) }\n}\nSystem.print(Plain.new(1).name) // Plain does not implement 'name'\n```\n\nClass setup in `vm.rs` resolves the superclass by scanning the module's\nvariables for a class object whose own name matches, so the imported\n`OtherBox` (named `Box`) wins over the local `Box`. It should take the\nvariable named `Box`. AOT's `plan_classes` resolves by variable name and\ngets it right.","files":null}]}